From 358cbcd2085eeea066728cd2f1c92867e2d2978c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:08:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0257 -- OPL window pacing is on by default again
 for a detected PicoGUS

WHY: patch 0256 turned the PicoGUS pacing default off pending an
investigation. The landed-build confirmation cell (dosags LAB-JOURNEYS 8.49)
had shown one silent SB IRQ above the limit, and whether pacing caused it was
not established. The pre-registered investigation has now run on the 486
(8.50 / 8.52, PACEI, round S): a same-binary ABBA with pacing on (K=128 by
hint) against off (0256's default). Silent IRQs were A [2, 3] against
B [2, 3], all at the known ambient/music decode stall, with every health row
clean in all four cells. The verdict is CLEARED: pacing adds no silent IRQs.
Meanwhile the unpaced peak bound read 168 in both off cells, so at least 152
OPL writes landed in one 2.57 ms PicoGUS drain window. That is the silent
buffer-overwrite risk (8.34) which pacing exists for, and paced it reads 144
(K + 16). The registered consequence of CLEARED (8.50 / 8.51) is to restore the
default.

WHAT: SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable's default K is again 128 for a detected
PicoGUS (0254's pgdetect), and 0 on every other card, as 0255 shipped it.
SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K and SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US are unchanged.
Two doc lines match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h | 2 +-
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
index e61d97930..6fe8cdb1e 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosmidi_tick.h
@@ -296,7 +296,7 @@ extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSMidiDeferStats4(Uint32 *dedupe_on, Uint3
    reads = dummy status reads after each address and data write. */
 extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSOplPacing(Uint32 *pgdetect, Uint32 *reads);
 /* DOS-PORT patch 0255: OPL arrival pacing and its witness. k = writes allowed per
-   window (0 = off; 0 by default on every card since patch 0256, a detected PicoGUS included;
+   window (0 = off; 128 by default on a detected PicoGUS (patch 0257), else 0;
    SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K), win_us = the window (default 2570, one PicoGUS
    drain period; SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US), waits and wait_us / wait_max_us
    = the pacing waits taken and their time (included in 0250's isr_sum),
diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 7899b00ab..a5e9b27e6 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -2249,14 +2249,14 @@ bool SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable(int kind)
         const char *e = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOS_MIDI_DEFER_DRAIN_STI");
         g_mdq_drain_sti = (e && e[0] == '0' && e[1] == 0) ? 0 : 1;
     }
-    { /* DOS-PORT patch 0255: window pacing -- off by default (0256; was on for a detected PicoGUS).
+    { /* DOS-PORT patch 0255: window pacing -- on for a detected PicoGUS, off elsewhere (0257).
          SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K=0 turns it off, N (16..1024) sets K on any OPL;
          SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US (500..20000) sets the window. */
         const char *e = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_K");
         const char *w = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PACE_WINDOW_US");
-        /* DOS-PORT patch 0256: off by default everywhere, a detected PicoGUS included, pending the
-           investigation of dosags LAB-JOURNEYS 8.49 (the hint still turns it on). */
-        Uint32 k = 0u;
+        /* DOS-PORT patch 0257: on by default again for a detected PicoGUS (K = 128), off
+           elsewhere -- 0256's pending investigation cleared it (dosags LAB-JOURNEYS 8.52). */
+        Uint32 k = (kind == 1 && g_dos_opl_pgdetect == 1) ? 128u : 0u;
         Uint32 win = 2570u;
         if (e && *e) {
             const long v = SDL_strtol(e, NULL, 10);
-- 
